WEBVTT

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:05.550
(ALL YELLING)

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.390
-(REX WHIMPERING)
-HAMM: Turn into the spin, Barbie!

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.670
(SCREAMS) My source of power!

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:18.390
No! Come back!
(YELLS) Hey!

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.270
Wait up! Hey! Come on! Slow down!

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.670
Dinosaur overboard!
Slow down! (CRIES OUT)

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.990
Remain seated, please.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.670
(RECITES IN SPANISH)

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.830
Ow! Listen to me. Listen to me.
You're not really a Space Ranger.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.430
You're a toy.
We're all toys. Do you hear me?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.230
Well, that should hold you
till the court martial.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:44.070
Let me go! You don't realize
what you're doing!

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.910
And this is the Buzz Lightyear aisle.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:52.190
In 1995, shortsighted retailers did not
order enough dolls to meet demand.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.390
-Hey, Buzz!
-Halt! Who goes there?

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.030
Quit clownin' around
and get in the car!

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.510
Buzz, Buzz, I know how to defeat Zurg!

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.830
-You do?
-Come on. I'll tell you on the way.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:08.430
No, no, guys! You've got the wrong
Buzz! You've got the wrong Buzz!

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.670
Say, where'd you get
the cool belt, Buzz?

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.230
Well, slotted pig,
they're standard issue.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.070
No!

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.830
(FLASH POPPING)

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.270
(AL CHUCKLING)

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.030
-It's like printing my own money.
-(PHONE RINGING)

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.350
-Yeah? What?
-(MAN SPEAKING, INDISTINCT)

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.670
Oh, oh. Mr. Konishi.
Yes, I have the pictures right here.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.390
In fact, I'm in the car right now on
my way to the office to fax them to you.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.430
I'm going through a tunnel!
I'm breakin' up!

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:47.270
Oh, wow! Will you look at me?
It's like I'm fresh out of the box!

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:51.510
Look at this stitching! Andy's gonna
have a hard time rippin' this! Hello!

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.630
Hi! Hello!

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.830
Great. Now you can go.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:01.230
Well, what a good idea.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.350
PETE: Woody, don't be mad at Jessie.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.070
She's been through
more than you know.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.350
Why not make amends
before you leave, huh?

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.630
It's the least you can do.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:32.630
(GROANS) All right.
But I don't know what good it'll do.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.230
Hey. Whatcha doin' way up here?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.150
Thought I'd get one last look at the
sun before I get packed away again.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.830
Look, Jessie.
I know you hate me for leaving,

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.230
but I have to go back.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.310
I'm still Andy's toy.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.790
Well, if you knew him,
you'd understand. Andy's a real...

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.670
Let me guess.
Andy's a real special kid.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.230
And to him, you're his buddy,
his best friend.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:09.670
And when Andy plays with you,
it's like even though you're not moving,

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.750
you feel like you're alive,
because that's how he sees you.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.310
How did you know that?

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.350
Because Emily was just the same.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.150
She was my whole world.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:28.470
